  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">RAP Vegetable Production &amp; Capacity Building Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Rural Agriculture Promoters (RAP) is a group of 46 community members located in Salayea Town in Lofa County. The goup produces cabbage, pepper, bitterball, and corn as well as running a village and savings loan. The funds for this project will be used to improve its organization and financial management capacity and well as increase production by constructing an office and storage warehouse, providing production tools and equipment, a working capital fund, and training to improve organizational and management operations.,</narrative>
  </description>
